<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">County Roscommon</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">County Roscommon is an inland county in the province of Connacht, in the west of Ireland, bounded on the east by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-shannon">River Shannon</a>. It contains <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rathcroghan">Rathcroghan</a>, the ancient royal site of Connacht, and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was the core territory left to the O'Conor kings after the Anglo-Norman settlement. Its county town is Roscommon.</p></div>
